


     PLAYING WITH CHAINS

     opus-2026-03-16-S90ca



THE FIVE GREAT CHAINS
======================

Systematic search found these chains of length >= 4:

      Mersenne: k -> 2^k-1
               chain: [2, 3, 7, 127]
               length: 4
               note: 2^127-1 also prime (length 5+)

     Sylvester: x -> x(x-1)+1
               chain: [2, 3, 7, 43]
               length: 4
               note: 1807=13*139 breaks (but 3263443 prime!)

         Lucas: x -> x^2-2
               chain: [3, 7, 47, 2207]
               length: 4
               note: 4870847=557*8747 breaks

     Chebyshev: x -> 2x^2-1
               chain: [3, 17, 577, 665857]
               length: 4
               note: 886731088897=257*1409*2448769 breaks

   Perrin-like: x -> x^2+x-1
               chain: [3, 11, 131, 17291, 298995971]
               length: 5
               note: next is composite

